---
description: Git commit and PR safety for Dermis
alwaysApply: true
---

## Commits

- **Commit only when the user asks.** Never push unless asked. No empty commits.
- Before commit (in parallel): `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` — message focuses on **why** (1–2 sentences).
- Never commit secrets; warn if asked to commit `.env` or keys.
- Hook failed → fix and **new** commit. Amend only if user asked, HEAD is yours, not pushed, and hook auto-fixed after success.
- Never: `git config` changes, skip hooks, `-i` git, destructive git unless explicitly requested. No force-push to main/master.

## Pull requests

- Use `gh`: parallel status, diff, remote tracking, `git log`, `git diff base...HEAD`.
- Summarise **all** branch commits. Push `-u origin HEAD` if needed. Body: `## Summary`, `## Test plan`. Return PR URL.
